$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 4.2. Reaction of S6O, prepared in situ by the
reaction of Cp2TiS5 (3) with SOCl2, with 2,3-diphenyl-1,3-butadiene (4).
A solution of SOCl2 (38.8 mg, 0.326mmol) in dichloromethane (1 mL) was
added to a solution of Cp2TiS5 (104.4mg, 0.309 mmol) in CS2 (15mL) at
-18°C under argon in the dark. After stirring for 30min, a solution of
2,3-diphenyl-1,3-butadiene (4) (124.7mg, 0.611 mmol) in dichloromethane
(10 mL) was added dropwise. The mixture was stirred for 2h at room
temperature and evaporated to dryness. Dibenzyl (34.3 mg, 0.188 mmol) was
added to the residue as the internal standard, and the 1H NMR spectrum of
the mixture indicated the presence of products. 1,2,3-trithiolane 14,
yield: 19%. Reactant: norbornene.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM in the dark
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Cyclohexasulfur monoxide (S6O) and cyclohexasulfur (S6) as
sulfur-transfer agents
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Ishii, Akihiko; Yamashita, Remi
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Sulfur Chemistry (2008), 29(3-4), 303-308

