equipped with a stir bar was swelled in anhydrous THF (2.0 mL).
Cp*RuCl(PPh3)2 (8.0 mg, 0.01 mmol) and phenyl acetylene (110 μL, 1.0
mmol) were added to the reaction mixture consecutively.13 The reaction
mixture was stirred gently at 70 °C for 8 h. General procedure A.
Cleavage, deprotection, and purification of peptides The peptides on
solid phase were washed with DMF (3x) and CH2Cl2 (3x) on a water
aspirator. The cleavage of peptides from resin was conducted using 96%
TFA, 2% water, and 2% triisopropylsilane (TIS) or triethylsilane (TES)
for 30-60 minutes. The solutions were concentrated by evaporation under
nitrogen and the peptides were precipitated with cold ether. The
precipitate was dissolved in water, filtered, and purified via reverse
phase HPLC (Vydac semipreparative C18, 10 x 250 mm, 5 μm particle size,
300 Å pore) using 20 min isocratic 100% buffer A (98% H2O, 2% MeCN, 0.06%
TFA), followed by a linear gradient of 0-50% buffer B (80% MeCN, 20% H2O,
0.05% TFA) in buffer A over 60 minutes, unless otherwise indicated.
Peptides were purified to homogeneity, as indicated by the presence of a
single peak on reinjection on analytical HPLC (Microsorb MV C18, 4.6 x
250 mm, 3-5 μm particle size, 100 Å pore). Peptide 112. Expected mass
677.3, observed mass (M + Na) 700.2, tR = 51.4 min.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, solid-supported reaction, Rink-amide resin used
