$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Resin-bound peptide 18' in a fritted tube was
swelled in anhydrous DMF (1.0 mL) and anhydrous THF (1.0 mL). Copper
iodide (CuI) (19.0 mg, 0.1 mmol) and DIPEA (174 μL, 1.0 mmol) were added,
followed by phenyl acetylene (110 μL, 1.0 mmol). The reaction mixture was
allowed to react with gentle mixing at room temperature for 8 h. General
procedure A. Cleavage, deprotection, and purification of peptides The
peptides on solid phase were washed with DMF (3x) and CH2Cl2 (3x) on a
water aspirator. The cleavage of peptides from resin was conducted using
96% TFA, 2% water, and 2% triisopropylsilane (TIS) or triethylsilane
(TES) for 30-60 minutes. The solutions were concentrated by evaporation
under nitrogen and the peptides were precipitated with cold ether. The
precipitate was dissolved in water, filtered, and purified via reverse
phase HPLC (Vydac semipreparative C18, 10 x 250 mm, 5 μm particle size,
300 Å pore) using 20 min isocratic 100% buffer A (98% H2O, 2% MeCN, 0.06%
TFA), followed by a linear gradient of 0-50% buffer B (80% MeCN, 20% H2O,
0.05% TFA) in buffer A over 60 minutes, unless otherwise indicated.
Peptides were purified to homogeneity, as indicated by the presence of a
single peak on reinjection on analytical HPLC (Microsorb MV C18, 4.6 x
250 mm, 3-5 μm particle size, 100 Å pore). Peptide 108 Expected mass
677.3, observed mass (M + Na) 700.2, tR = 50.9 min.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, solid-supported reaction, Rink-amide resin used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Proline Editing: A General and Practical Approach to the Synthesis of
Functionally and Structurally Diverse Peptides. Analysis of Steric versus
Stereoelectronic Effects of 4-Substituted Prolines on Conformation within
Peptides
