$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM The reaction of 14 with 15 was monitored by GC, using a ten-fold excess
of 14. Compounds 14 (100 mg, 0.741 mmol based on 80% purity), 15 (9.2 μL,
0.074 mmol), and dodecane (17 μL, 0.074 mmol) were dissolved in THF (0.74
mL) at 25°C. Aliquots of the mixture were diluted with 1 mL of CH2Cl2 and
analyzed by GC every minute until 50% conversion. Dodecane was used as an
internal standard to quantify the consumption of 15.
